      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Assert console output and cover all `cable_curr` boundary and `NULL`-entry cases**\n\n`command_cable()` always returns `EC_SUCCESS` (`0`) for a valid port regardless of whether it prints `\"Cable Current: 3A\"`, `\"Cable Current: 5A\"`, or `\"Cable Current: Invalid\"`. As a result, `zassert_ok(shell_execute_cmd(get_ec_shell(), \"pdcable 0\"))` only checks the return code and would still pass even if the `\"Cable Current: ...\"` output regressed.\n\nAdditionally, `(vbus_cur \u003c ARRAY_SIZE(cable_curr) \u0026\u0026 cable_curr[vbus_cur])` has `ARRAY_SIZE(cable_curr) \u003d\u003d 3` (`{ NULL, \"3A\", \"5A\" }`), so testing only `USB_VBUS_CUR_3A` (`1`) and `USB_VBUS_CUR_RES_3` (`3`) leaves two key boundary/clause cases untested:\n- **`USB_VBUS_CUR_RES_0` (`0`)**: Isolates the `\u0026\u0026 cable_curr[vbus_cur]` `NULL`-entry check when `vbus_cur \u003c ARRAY_SIZE(cable_curr)` is true (`\"Cable Current: Invalid\"`).\n- **`USB_VBUS_CUR_5A` (`2`, i.e., `ARRAY_SIZE(cable_curr) - 1`)**: Tests the upper in-bounds boundary (`N - 1`) so an off-by-one bound would be caught (`\"Cable Current: 5A\"`).\n\nUse `CHECK_CONSOLE_CMD` (already included via `\"test/drivers/utils.h\"` and used earlier in this file) to assert both `EC_SUCCESS` and the printed `\"Cable Current: ...\"` substring across all four `enum usb_vbus_cur` values:\n\n```c\n\t/* Test valid, NULL-entry, and out-of-bounds vbus_cur values */\n\tdev_disc \u003d\n\t\tpd_get_am_discovery_and_notify_access(0, TCPCI_MSG_SOP_PRIME);\n\tdev_disc-\u003eidentity.product_t1.p_rev20.vbus_cur \u003d USB_VBUS_CUR_RES_0;\n\tCHECK_CONSOLE_CMD(\"pdcable 0\", \"Cable Current: Invalid\", EC_SUCCESS);\n\tdev_disc-\u003eidentity.product_t1.p_rev20.vbus_cur \u003d USB_VBUS_CUR_3A;\n\tCHECK_CONSOLE_CMD(\"pdcable 0\", \"Cable Current: 3A\", EC_SUCCESS);\n\tdev_disc-\u003eidentity.product_t1.p_rev20.vbus_cur \u003d USB_VBUS_CUR_5A;\n\tCHECK_CONSOLE_CMD(\"pdcable 0\", \"Cable Current: 5A\", EC_SUCCESS);\n\tdev_disc-\u003eidentity.product_t1.p_rev20.vbus_cur \u003d USB_VBUS_CUR_RES_3;\n\tCHECK_CONSOLE_CMD(\"pdcable 0\", \"Cable Current: Invalid\", EC_SUCCESS);\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/3aaf00a0-ca27-4f84-a2b4-6d47a8c3028f)",
